00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
The Poughkeepsie Tapes is a 2007 American pseudo-documentary horror film written, directed, and
edited by John Erick Dowdle from a story he co-wrote with his brother Drew Dowdle.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
It revolves around a serial killer's murders in Poughkeepsie, New York, told
through interviews and footage from a cache of the killer's snuff films.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The film premiered at the 2007 Tribeca Film Festival, but had a troubled release history; it was originally slated for
theatrical release by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer in February 2008, but was removed from the release schedule.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The film had a brief video-on-demand release in 2014,
but remained unavailable on home media.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
In October 2017, the film was released and
remastered on DVD and Blu-ray by Shout!

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
Factory via the newly-revived Orion Pictures.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film explores themes of mask, pedophilia,
stockholm syndrome, suffering, sadism.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
